//  1 / 2 = 0 rem 1 (MSB) -> Result: 1101_2`},{question:"How do you convert a fractional Decimal number (e.g. 0.625) to Binary?",shortAnswer:"Repeatedly multiply the fraction by 2, record the integer carry, and read the carries top to bottom.",explanation:"Multiplying by 2 shifts the highest fractional power ($2^{-1}$) into the units integer position. Recording each integer part and repeating with the remaining fraction generates bits after the radix point ($b_{-1}, b_{-2}, b_{-3}$) in top-to-bottom order.",hint:"Integer parts generated during multiplication become the fractional digits.",level:"moderate",codeExample:`// Converting 0.625 to binary:
