//    3 / 16 =  0 R 3 -> 0x3E8`},{question:"What is the ASCII binary and hex encoding of the character 'A'?",shortAnswer:"Decimal 65 -> Binary (01000001)₂ -> Hexadecimal 0x41.",explanation:"In standard 7-bit/8-bit ASCII, uppercase 'A' is mapped to decimal code 65. $65 = 64 + 1 = 01000001_2 = 0x41$. Lowercase 'a' is 97 ($65 + 32 = 01100001_2 = 0x61$). The 6th bit (bit 5) toggles case!",hint:"Bit 5 = 1 for lowercase, Bit 5 = 0 for uppercase.",level:"moderate",codeExample:`// In C:
